{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1765117,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"amber-dark_un","paid":0,"title":"Netritva - Case Analysis Challenge","festival_id":null,"organization_id":559,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-09-30T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-25T22:00:20+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/netrivita-case-analysis-challenge-institute-of-management-technology-imt-nagpur-1765117","region":"hybrid","details":"<p><strong>Overview:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The Institution Industry Partnership Cell of IMT Nagpur is excited to extend a warm invitation to students from B-schools across India and beyond for the Case Analysis Challenge (CAC). As one of India's premier B-schools, IMT Nagpur is proud to present this unique opportunity for students from various specialisations, including Business, Finance, Marketing, HR, and Operations, to come together and address the most pressing challenges in the Indian HR ecosystem.<\/p>\n<p>The Case Analysis Challenge is a multi-phased competition that kicks off with a stimulating Quiz Competition, followed by two rounds of in-depth Case Study Analysis. Participants will have the chance to delve into real-world HR issues and present their comprehensive solutions. The winning team, along with the runner-up, will be rewarded with exciting prizes after the final round.<\/p>\n<p>This competition is your chance to think beyond your capacity and contribute innovative ideas to tackle current HR challenges in India. Join us on this journey to maximise your potential and emerge as a winner of The Case Analysis Challenge by the Institution Industry Partnership Cell of IMT Nagpur.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Case Analysis Challenge is open to all students at all B-schools PAN India across all years of study and specialisation.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Guidelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>There should be a team of exactly 3 members in each team.<\/li>\n<li>Cross-year teams are allowed.<\/li>\n<li>Cross-specialisation teams are allowed.<\/li>\n<li>Cross-campus teams are not allowed.<\/li>\n<li>Any changes to the team constitution will not be allowed post-registration.<\/li>\n<li>Any person cannot be a part of more than one team.<\/li>\n<li>The meetings will be conducted through MS Teams.<\/li>\n<li>The candidate should join the meeting 10 minutes prior to their presentation slot.<\/li>\n<li>All the PPTs need to be uploaded to the Google Forms.<\/li>\n<li>The organiser's\/judges' decision will be final.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Dress Code:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Students are required to be in business formals (Blazer is compulsory for both boys and girls, and a tie is compulsory for boys).<\/li>\n<li>Students have to be properly groomed, i.e., boys need to have their hair and beard neatly trimmed, and girls need to have their hair neatly tied back.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Competition Structure:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>After the registration period concludes, registered teams will be required to participate in the initial round, which is the Quiz round.<\/li>\n<li>Teams that successfully qualify from the first round will receive an email containing a link to a meeting where they will be briefed on the subsequent rounds of the event.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round Details:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>One member of each team has to appear for the Quiz round.<\/li>\n<li>The quiz will be of 30 minutes.<\/li>\n<li>It is mandatory for all the registered teams to attempt the online quiz.<\/li>\n<li>In case a team does not attempt the quiz round, the team's score will be considered null and void.<\/li>\n<li>The quiz will include a mix of questions that assess students' verbal, logical, and quantitative skills to gauge their critical thinking abilities.<\/li>\n<li>The quiz questions will be in a multiple-choice format (MCQs).<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 1 - Presentation:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All the qualifying teams based on the quiz will move to Round 1.<\/li>\n<li>The shortlisted teams will be provided with a case.<\/li>\n<li>The case will be mailed to the team leader.<\/li>\n<li>The presentation will be made in front of the faculty of IMT Nagpur.<\/li>\n<li>The naming convention of the PPT should be CAC_Teamname_Round1.<\/li>\n<li>Each team will be given a total of 12 minutes: 10 minutes for presentation and 2 minutes for Q&amp;A.<\/li>\n<li>It is mandatory for all the team members to be present for the Presentation.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2 - Final Presentation:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The shortlisted teams will move to Round 2.<\/li>\n<li>The teams that move to Round 2 are expected to offer a comprehensive analysis and exhibit creative thinking when presenting the case before the panel of judges.<\/li>\n<li>Each team will be given a total of 15 minutes: 12 minutes for presentation and 3 minutes for Q&amp;A.<\/li>\n<li>It is mandatory for all the team members to be present for the Presentation.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rewards and Prizes:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The winning teams and runners-up will be awarded gift vouchers.<\/li>\n<li>The winning team will be awarded gift vouchers worth Rs 18,000.<\/li>\n<li>Runners-up team will be awarded gift vouchers worth Rs 12,000.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":"Prizes worth \u20b9 30,000","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":33429690,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-03T01:54:19+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-07T20:47:29+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"case_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"heRjv6q","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":1,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":1,"disp